{"name":"Glow in the Dark","hex":"#befdb7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glow-in-the-dark","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["glowing; glowy"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow-in-the-dark"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bioluminescence","blocks":[{"text":"Bioluminescence is the production of light by an organism as the result of a chemiluminescence reaction. It occurs in a wide variety of organisms, including marine vertebrates and invertebrates, terrestrial arthropods such as fireflies, some fungi, and microorganisms such as some bacteria and dinoflagellates. In some animals, the light is bacteriogenic, produced by symbiotic bacteria such as those from the genus Vibrio; in others, it is autogenic, produced by the animals themselves. Bioluminescence has evolved independently at least 94 times, first emerging in octocorals some 540 million years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Photinus_pyralis_Firefly_glowing.jpg/330px-Photinus_pyralis_Firefly_glowing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioluminescence","wikidata":"Q179924"},{"title":"Chemiluminescence","blocks":[{"text":"Chemiluminescence is the emission of light (luminescence) as the result of a chemical reaction, i.e. a chemical reaction resulting in a flash or glow of light. A standard example of chemiluminescence in the laboratory setting is the luminol test wherein blood is indicated by luminescence upon contact with iron in hemoglobin. A light stick also emits light by chemiluminescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Chemoluminescent_reaction.jpg/330px-Chemoluminescent_reaction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemiluminescence","wikidata":"Q2931725"},{"title":"Glow in the Dark (book)","blocks":[{"text":"Glow in the Dark is a biographical photo essay about Kanye West's Glow in the Dark Tour published by Rizzoli USA on October 20, 2009. Authored by West, the book was designed by Base and features 400 exclusive images taken on the tour by Australian-American photographer Nabil Elderkin, who had previously directed several of West's music videos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Glow-in-the-dark-kanye-west.png/330px-Glow-in-the-dark-kanye-west.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glow_in_the_Dark_(book)","wikidata":"Q5572228"},{"title":"Glow in the Dark (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Glow in the Dark\" is a song by British-Irish boy band The Wanted. It was released as their thirteenth single on 23 March 2014 from their third studio album Word of Mouth (2013) and was the last single they released before they went on a hiatus. The song received its first radio play on 17 February 2014 and reached number 177 on the UK Singles Chart, becoming their lowest-charting single to date."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/The_Wanted_-_Glow_in_the_Dark_%28Official_Single_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glow_in_the_Dark_(song)","wikidata":"Q16251408"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg/330px-Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg/330px-Lampyris_noctiluca.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Female glowworm, Lampyris noctiluca","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALampyris_noctiluca.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Aequorea4.jpg/500px-Aequorea4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Aequorea4.jpg/500px-Aequorea4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Osamu Shimomura isolated the photoprotein aequorin and its cofactor coelenterazine from the crystal jelly Aequorea victoria in 1961.[10]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAequorea4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png/500px-Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png/500px-Firefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Protein structure of the luciferase of the firefly Photinus pyralis. The enzyme is a much larger molecule than luciferin.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirefly_Luciferase_Crystal_Structure.rsh.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mycena_chlorophos.jpg/500px-Mycena_chlorophos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mycena_chlorophos.jpg/1280px-Mycena_chlorophos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Mycena_chlorophos.jpg/500px-Mycena_chlorophos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mycena chlorophos, a bioluminescent mushroom. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMycena_chlorophos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Squid_Counterillumination.png/500px-Squid_Counterillumination.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src"